      "failingExample": "Counterexample 1 - Urgency 'darurat': priority_in_database='darurat' (should be NULL)\nCounterexample 2 - Urgency 'tinggi': priority_in_database='tinggi' (should be NULL)\nCounterexample 3 - Urgency 'sedang': priority_in_database='sedang' (should be NULL)\nCounterexample 4 - Urgency 'rendah': priority_in_database='rendah' (should be NULL)\n\nBug Root Cause: PublicReportService.php line 56 uses fallback logic:\n'priority' => $validated['priority'] ?? $validated['urgency']\n\nSince public form submission does NOT include 'priority' field (it's admin-only), the code falls back to urgency value. This causes priority to mirror urgency instead of being independent/NULL.\n\nTest Documentation: Created property-based unit test (tests/Unit/PriorityPersistenceBugTest.php) that demonstrates:\n1. Bug analysis confirms the fallback logic exists in current code\n2. Bug affects all urgency values (rendah, sedang, tinggi, darurat)\n3. All counterexamples show priority=urgency instead of priority=NULL\n4. Expected fix: Change line 56 to 'priority' => null\n\nTest Results: 4/4 unit tests passed, confirming bug condition analysis is correct.",
